CHECK 2  CLOSED FORM.  lam_slice = sqrt(m^2 (m^2+4)),  so lam_slice/(2 m1) = sqrt(m^2+4)/2
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  derivation: C_slice(k_s) = (1/L)sum_{k_t} 1/(m^2+lam(k_s)+lam(k_t)) -> (1/2pi)int_0^2pi dk_t
             /(m^2+lam(k_s)+2-2cos k_t) = 1/sqrt((m^2+lam)(m^2+lam+4));  sup at k_s=0.
  => the lattice (a=1) artefact is EXACTLY the time-direction dispersion; the factor is
     sqrt(m^2+4)/2 -> 1 as m -> 0 (continuum), and it is 1.06 at m=0.7, 1.12 at m=1.
