==============================================================================
VERDICT (witness only; the theorem is in R1-BRIDGE.md S1)
==============================================================================
  lam_conf <= lam_slice = 2*m1 holds at every point; the loss is (i) the factor 2 = the
  1/2-kinetic convention (not a loss: matched metrics give 1), (ii) the factor m/2 between
  the Gibbs measure and the vacuum measure (a REAL loss, unbounded as m->0).
  Hence: the direction of the inference is safe -- a positive uniform lower bound on the
  Gibbs Poincare constant implies a positive gap; only its MAGNITUDE is weak.
==============================================================================
